@* The demos on the Architecture page: three projects built on the framework, each as a customer's own would be. *@
<Band Id="demos" Kicker="demos · built on it">
    <h3>A demo is someone's own project.</h3>
    <p class="lede">Each holds what a customer's would: an identity, the programs that start the framework's hosts, a web app, its evals, config, Docker, the deploy and its tests. Nothing in <code>src/</code> knows a demo exists.</p>
    <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="panel">
            <h4>louis-agent</h4>
            <p>The coding agent, and this site.</p>
            <p class="muted"><code>louis-agent.identity.coding</code> who the coding agent is · <code>louis-agent.identity.expert</code> the guide in the corner · <code>louis-agent.identity.triage</code> the team that will triage a service's errors, a manager with three roles ·<code>louis-agent.coding-catalog</code> the identities and packs it loads · <code>louis-agent.coding-api</code>, <code>louis-agent.coding-cli</code>, <code>louis-agent.coding-acp</code>, <code>louis-agent.coding-mcp</code> and <code>louis-agent.coding-eval-runner</code>, one small program per host · <code>louis-agent.code-review</code> this web app · <code>louis-agent.orchestrator</code> a proof of concept that has the coding agent fix a service's errors · <code>louis-agent.film-export</code> renders this site's films to WebP</p>
        </article>
        <article class="panel">
            <h4>puls</h4>
            <p>The South African assistant, live on mypuls.co.za.</p>
            <p class="muted"><code>louis-agent.identity.puls</code> who Puls is, its specialists as roles · <code>louis-agent.identity.puls.evals</code> and <code>louis-agent.identity.puls.judges</code> what proves it · <code>louis-agent.host-packs</code> the one project that names its packs · <code>louis-agent.puls-api</code> and <code>louis-agent.puls-eval-runner</code> its programs · <code>louis-agent.puls</code> its web app</p>
        </article>
        <article class="panel">
            <h4>starter</h4>
            <p>The smallest site, and what <code>dotnet new louis-site</code> makes.</p>
            <p class="muted"><code>louis-agent.starter</code> the web app · <code>louis-agent.starter-api</code> its program</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</Band>
